From d297f60c852dab7dd4fd5a8cfd4ed0d02b071f2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:41:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Namespace compiler snapshot caches by source version

Upstream base: 2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5 with the unchanged
ordered ten-patch compiler stack, head454202b2ba8d0cf10b8caf434a956755e039483f
and pre-metadata treebae5fe12b58cdf364efeccbabc04cd08205c43b9.

Rationale: different compiler snapshots advertising0.1.15 can select the same
persistent JIT entries when optional library stamping is disabled. Give this
snapshot an immutable local package version, used by its existing cache key
and namespace. The suffix names the pre-metadata source tree, not itself.

Quality: VERSION is the only changed file. Compiler passes, kernels, arithmetic,
models and policies are unchanged. Existing caches are preserved rather than
cleared or silently reused across compiler identities.

Tests: source-only version provider under NO_VERSION_LABEL=1, PEP440/wheel
parsing, source-derived CMake boundaries and cache-key/namespace disjointness.
Actual Linux wheel/image, installed identity, full release/functional gates
and both complete metric boots remain required; no serving gain is claimed.

Upstream status: local experiment; not submitted upstream.
---
 VERSION | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/VERSION b/VERSION
index c34958a4..43f1e5ca 100644
--- a/VERSION
+++ b/VERSION
@@ -1 +1 @@
-0.1.15
+0.1.15+snapshot.bae5fe12b58cdf364efeccbabc04cd08205c43b9
-- 
2.54.0 (Apple Git-157)
